  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A block of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> is kept stationary on a smooth inclined plane by applying a minimum horizontal force <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> as shown in figure.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0078_8158feef466b.png\" style=\"width: 172px; height: 200px;\" /></p><p>The value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi></math>.</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "12",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0078_56a131cac0ed.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 204px;\" /><img src=\"assets\\st0078_7f1bbcbfcb50.png\" style=\"width: 160px; height: 164px;\" /></p><p>Balancing the forces in horizontal&nbsp;direction&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>F</mi></math></p><p>And balancing the forces in vertical direction&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>tan</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>tan</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>12</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>. Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math></p>"
  }
